check::lock_no_auth

  × this `lock` has no way out: nothing in it calls `auth.submit`
   ╭─[lock_popup.strand:5:1]
 4 │ export state locked = false
 5 │ lock {
   · ──┬─
   ·   ╰── only `auth.submit` can unlock the session
 6 │   open: <-> locked
   ╰────
  help: add a password field: `input { type: password; text: <-> secret; on activate { if secret !
        = "" { auth.submit(secret) }; secret = "" } }` (an empty Return is not sent: with
        pam_faillock it would count as a failed login)

